# Gitchangelog commit messages

## When this applies

Repo root has `.gitchangelog.rc`. Commit subjects become HISTORY sections, then GitHub release “What’s new” via `make release-*` / `scripts/release.sh`.

## Format

```text
[TAG] Imperative user-facing summary.
```

| Tag | HISTORY section | Use for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `[ADD]` | Added | New capability the user did not have |
| `[FIX]` | Fixed | Bug or broken behavior |
| `[REF]` | Changed | Behavior/API/UX change that is not a new feature |
| `[DEL]` | Removed | Removal of a feature or path |

When ADD vs FIX is ambiguous, default to `[FIX]`.

## Exclude from changelog

Non-user-facing work (deps, lint, prettier, fleet sync, CI plumbing) must not inflate release notes:

- Append `!cosmetic`, `!refactor`, or `!wip` to the subject, **or**
- Use a `CI:` prefix (already ignored by `.gitchangelog.rc`).

Example: `Sync maintainer ops from fleet. !cosmetic`

## Subject craft

- User-visible outcome, not a file inventory.
- Terse imperative; ideally <=50 chars, hard-capped at 72 (including the tag).
- Sentence case; trailing period is fine (gitchangelog applies `ucfirst` + final dot).
- No AI attribution, filler, or diff restatement.

## PR titles

PR titles may stay `type: description` (Conventional-style). Only **commit subjects** feed gitchangelog / HISTORY.

## Examples

Good:

```text
[ADD] X Aggregator utility for timeline exports.
[FIX] Spanish copy and grammar in X Aggregator.
[REF] Redesign homepage content sections.
[DEL] Remove legacy MCP card build path.
chore: sync maintainer ops !cosmetic
```

Bad (land in Other or clutter release notes):

```text
fix: pin eslint to ^9.28.0
Chore: apply rosey-maintainer fleet sync.
Fixing bugs
```
